-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",367,{
[11713]="700608E9\n1\tTalk to Waltney Maythorn III\tWaltney Maythorn III is in Tornhad. Garan Maythorn has asked you to let her son know that his parents are nearly to Tornhad.\n2\tCollect fresh meat (total: 8)\tBoar meat can be collected from forest-boars in the Angle. Waltney Maythorn III has asked you to collect fresh boar meat to help fill his larder before his parents arrive.\n3\tReturn to Waltney Maythorn III\tWaltney Maythorn III, called Thorn, is in Tornhad. You should bring the fresh meat to Thorn.\n",
[11714]="7002F91C\n1\tCollect hides from Norcrofts brown-bears (total: 5)\tNorcrofts brown bears dwell among the trees and rocks east along the river. Caddabrand has asked you to collect hides from brown bears to prove that you are capable of more profitable ventures.\n2\tReturn to Caddabrand with the brown bear-hides\tCaddabrand waits at his encampment, west and south of the river crossing. You have collected the brown bear-hides sought by the scout Caddabrand.\n",
[11715]="700687C6\n1\tCheck the Dahâl Huliz's north-western entrance\tAkhamâl has told you to check the north-western entrance of the Dahâl Huliz for Belhax.\n2\tExamine the crate\030Examine the puddle\tYou have found a leaking crate at the Dahâl Huliz's north-western entrance. Belhax is nowhere in sight. You should examine it and the puddle it's leaving.\n3\tFollow the wine droplet trail\tYou have found Belhax's wine delivery, but not him. A trail of wine droplets leads you further around the Tor-gardens pool. You should follow it.\n4\tFollow the wine droplet trail\tYou have found Belhax's wine delivery, but not him. A trail of wine droplets leads you further around the Tor-gardens pool. You should follow it.\n5\tTalk to Belhax\tYou have found Belhax at the gazebo in the center of the Tor-gardens pool! You should try to talk to him.\n6\tTalk to Akhamâl at the Dahâl Huliz\tYou've found Belhax safe and sound. You should tell Akhamâl back at the Dahâl Huliz.\n",
[11716]="70028257\n1\tAttend the Auction\tBedwur is at Avardin, central to the Starkmoor. Bedwur is waiting for you to begin the auction.\n2\tTalk to Bedwur at Avardin\tBedwur is at Avardin, central to the Starkmoor. Bedwur will want to discuss the events of the Auction.\n",
[11717]="7002822C\n1\tTalk to Bedwur in Avardin\tBedwur is in the centre of Avardin at the auction-platform. Andras asked you to speak with Bedwur regarding the auction.\n",
[11718]="70027178\n1\tDefeat the Great Avanc\tThe Great Avanc is at its lair in Lhun Avanc. You should defeat the Great Avanc, terror of Carreglyn.\n2\tTalk to Gwilum in Barnavon\tGwilum is at Barnavon, north of Lhun Avanc. You should tell Gwilum of the death of the Great Avanc.\n",
[11719]="7006C5F1\n1\tSpeak with Raphûz near Telperiën's Wall\tMake your way to Raphûz in the shadow of Telperiën's Wall and ask the young man why he is sullen.\n2\tSearch the area around the road for Raphûz's pack\tRaphûz confessed to dropping his pack while investigating something he saw in the distance while travelling with the caravan. He asked you to follow the road to the south-west and search for his missing pack.\n3\tInvestigate the person watching you to the north-west\tYou found the location Raphûz described where he lost his pack and noticed what looked like a person watching you to the north-west. You should investigate.\n4\tCollect Raphûz's pack\tYou saw something to the north-west and went to investigate. When you arrived you did not find a person. You did, however, find a pack.\n5\tReturn the pack to Raphûz at Telperiën's Wall\tYou took the pack from the ground and made certain it was Raphûz's. You can find no signs that anyone was standing here a moment ago. Return the pack to Raphûz.\n6\tTalk to Kizeri\tRaphûz is grateful to you for returning his pack. He asks you to go to Kizeri and tell her that you helped him as she asked.\n",
[11720]="7003FBFE\n1\tSearch the shores for a Fish Ball\tCalembel is to the north-east of Dol Amroth. Torchuil asked you to go to Calembel and wait for a fish ball. Once you found it, you were to fish as quickly as possible.\n2\tCatch fish (total: 3)\tThe fish have balled up. Catch as many as you can. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Torchuil\tTorchuil is in Dol Amroth. Torchuil will be pleased to see the fish you were able to catch.\n",
[11721]="70066733\n1\tExamine the lumber pile\030Examine the cloth\030Examine the barricade\tA villager wants to know what might be found at the nearby bandit camp. Investigate the bandit camp west of Dínadab.\n2\tTalk to Peran\tTell Peran that you have examined the supplies at the camp.\n",
[11722]="7004BEB0\n1\tCount bandit stash (total: 8)\tThe Haradrim commander's stash can be found in Fushaum Bal South. You should count the stash to make sure it is all there.\n2\tTalk to the Haradrim Commander\tThe Haradrim Commander can be found at Fushaum Bal South. You should talk to the Haradrim Commander.\n",
[11723]="70050E1F\n1\tDefeat Hunulf's Bane\tYou should find and defeat the wolverine.\n2\tDefeat Hunulf's Bane\tYou should find and defeat the wolverine.\n3\tReturn to Hunulf\tYou should return to Hunulf, who can be found in Skoghús, in the Thornholt woods.\n",
[11724]="700544D7\n1\tDefeat the Bane of Rhûn in Mordor Besieged\tOnce he was a great king in lands far to the east, accustomed to rule and unwilling to bend the knee to any other. But then came a giver of gifts and a promiser of power, and upon accepting these lures, the great king changed. No longer did he rule his lands with mercy, and neither did he remain in his own kingdom. He became Rhûn's bane, and by that name came he to be known as the Bane of Rhûn, and elsewhere.\n2\tDefeat the Bane of Rhûn in Mordor Besieged\tOnce he was a great king in lands far to the east, accustomed to rule and unwilling to bend the knee to any other. But then came a giver of gifts and a promiser of power, and upon accepting these lures, the great king changed. No longer did he rule his lands with mercy, and neither did he remain in his own kingdom. He became Rhûn's bane, and by that name came he to be known as the Bane of Rhûn, and elsewhere.\n3\tThe Bane of Rhûn, defeated but enduring\tOnce he was a great king in lands far to the east, accustomed to rule and unwilling to bend the knee to any other. But then came a giver of gifts and a promiser of power, and upon accepting these lures, the great king changed. No longer did he rule his lands with mercy, and neither did he remain in his own kingdom. He became Rhûn's bane, and by that name came he to be known as the Bane of Rhûn, and elsewhere.\n",
[11725]="70028245\n1\tTalk to someone in the Dunbog\tDunbog lies to the south-west of Starkmoor. Eva told you of a terror in the swamps of Dunland who comes in the night and steals away orphans and lost children.\n",
[11726]="70043B49\n1\tTalk to Bingo at Haldirith, in Thinglad along the Great River\tBingo has decided to travel along the banks of the Great River, south of Lothlórien, and wants to meet you at the Elf outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad.\n2\tFind an Elf at Haldirith willing to help you with Bingo's ink shortage\tBingo has asked you to speak to the Elves at Haldirith, in Thinglad along the Great River, about the possibility of borrowing an inkpot.\n3\tCollect river-side reeds north-east of Haldirith (total: 8)\030Collect dark mud north-east of Haldirith (total: 4)\tRiver-side reeds and dark mud can be found to the north-east of Haldirith, along the banks of the Great River.\n4\tGrind ingredients into pigment using the grinding stone in Haldirith\tMaervadhor has told you to collect a number of ingredients which you can use to make a high-quality ink. The next step involves grinding them into pigment at a stone in Haldirith.\n5\tAdd the pigment you created to the bucket of water in Haldirith\tMaervadhor explained the ink-making process to you, and the next step is to add the pigment you created to the nearby bucket of water.\n6\tBring the ink to Bingo at Haldirith\tBingo is at the Elf-outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad on the banks of the Great River. You have replenished Bingo's supply of ink, and should learn what the hobbit wishes to do next.\n7\tTalk to Maervadhor at Haldirith\tMaervadhor is at the Elf-outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad, along the banks of the Great River. Bingo has asked for Maervadhor's recommendation of exciting places to visit along the Great River.\n8\tFind Foul-maw's Den, south-east of Haldirith\030Find the Old Burrows, south of Haldirith\tMaervadhor recommended that Bingo explore the Old Burrows, to the south of Haldirith, and Foul-maw's Den, to the south-east of Haldirith, if he seeks adventures worth writing.\n9\tTalk to Bingo in Haldirith\tBingo is at the Elf outpost of Haldirith, in Thinglad along the banks of the Great River.\n",
[11727]="70033031\n1\tDefeat Rûgh and burn his banner\tRûgh and his banner can be found in the barracks of Uzbad-bakân in Zelem-melek. You should defeat Rûgh and burn his banner.\n2\tDefeat Rûgh\030Destroy Rûgh's banner\tRûgh and his banner can be found in the barracks of Uzbad-bakân in Zelem-melek. You should defeat Rûgh and burn his banner.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated the leader of Uzbad-bakân, an evil Orc named Rûgh. With his banner destroyed and his constant chanting silenced, the Orcs of Zelem-melek will be less organized in their attacks.\n",
[11728]="7005B1F6\n1\tBurn Orkish banners (total: 5)\tDurshulot lies on the middle tier to the north-west of Aslíf. Rékkur believes that burning the Orkish banners at Durshulot will diminish the morale among Gorgar's forces.\n2\tTalk to Rékkur in Aslíf\tRékkur is stationed in Aslíf and will want to hear that the deed is done.\n",
[11729]="70044535\n1\tJoin the Finder's Gathering\tBergil can be found in front of the Old Guest-house, in the First Circle, just south of the City Gates. Talk to Bergil to join the children in the Finder's Gathering.\n",
[11730]="7001AD2B\n1\tDefeat Durshâtaz\tDurshâtaz can be found at Krul Lugu, below Iavassúl's Watch. Iavssúl has asked you to find and defeat the Orc-leader Durshâtaz. He suggests trying to attract his attention as he roams between the two fortresses.\n2\tTalk to Iavassúl at Iavassúl's Watch\tIavassúl is at Iavassúl's Watch, above Krul Lugu. You should return to Iavassúl with news of your victory.\n",
[11731]="7006835D\n1\tDefeat Ghadamût and collect its maw\tTevurin directed you to look along the sands near the shore east of the expedition camp in search of the great ancient crocodile, Ghadamût. Defeat the crocodile and collect its jaws.\n2\tTevurin directed you to look along the shore south and east of the expedition camp during the day in search of the great ancient crocodile, Ghadamût. Defeat the crocodile, collect its jaws, and return it to Tevurin.\t\n",
[11732]="70010167\n1\tTravel with Faelbenn to the Rammas Deluon\tFaelbenn is near Gath Forthnír. The Ranger Faelbenn has asked you to help him defeat the sorceresses of Angmar who are strengthening the watching-stones of Rammas Deluon and move against the Angmarim reinforcements.\n2\tTalk to Faelbenn\tFaelbenn is near Gath Forthnír. Faelbenn waits to speak with you again.\n",
[11733]="70051B6E\n1\tTalk to Wyn\tTalk to the children of Winterhome.\n2\tTalk to Liddy\030Talk to the Queen of Cluckland\tTalk to the children of Winterhome.\n3\tTalk to Griff\030Talk to Corr\030Talk to Una\tTalk to the children of Winterhome.\n4\tCapture the Tower of Grumpwood!\t\n5\tCapture the Keep of Cluckland!\t\n6\tCapture Fortress of Frostlake!\t\n",
[11734]="70051B6F\n1\tComplete The Battle at Frostbluff\tComplete The Battle at Frostbluff.\n",
[11735]="7005D39E\n1\tDefeat hobgoblins (total: 12)\tAnatrâd is in north-eastern Clovengap. You should defeat hobgoblins at Anatrâd.\n",
[11736]="70010166\n1\tTravel with Firingal to Aughaire\tFiringal is near Gath Forthnír. Mordirith's host approaches Aughaire in the western reaches of Angmar. The Ranger Firingal has asked you to aid in the defence of Aughaire.\n2\tTalk to Firingal\tFiringal is near Gath Forthnír. You should speak with Firingal regarding the defence of Aughaire.\n",
[11737]="7002140F\n1\tReport to Rodelleth in Gathbúrz\tRodelleth is encamped at the captured tower of Thangúlhad in Gathbúrz, east of Ost Galadh. Fuirgam has asked you to join Rodelleth's forces in battle against the Orcs of Gathbúrz before the gates of the tower of Dol Guldur.\n",
[11738]="70033CA2\n1\tDrag down the banners and define your terms ([see journal]/2)\tEasterling banners line the stairs, each establishing a different term for the battle to take place under.\n2\tDefeat the Olog-hai Champions\tThe Olog-hai champions must be defeated for the siege to be broken. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[11739]="70033CA3\n1\tDrag down the banners and define your terms ([see journal]/4)\tEasterling banners line the stairs, each establishing a different term for the battle to take place under.\n2\tDefeat the Olog-hai Champions\tThe Olog-hai champions must be defeated for the siege to be broken. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[11740]="70033CA4\n1\tDrag down the banners and define your terms ([see journal]/6)\tEasterling banners line the stairs, each establishing a different term for the battle to take place under. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tDefeat the Olog-hai Champions\tThe Olog-hai champions must be defeated for the siege to be broken. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n",
[11741]="7005CE64\n1\tDefeat Angmarim (total: 12)\tGarânashmar perches across Kurdushâlak, in north-western Clovengap. Rúdin has asked you to defeat Angmarim at Garânashmar.\n2\tReturn to Rúdin\tRúdin is in Bazanmanar in north-eastern Clovengap. You should tell Rúdin that you have defeated many of the Angmarim.\n",
[11742]="7006EEDA\n1\tSpeak with Mizâdi in southern Imhûlar outside Nisigurûm\tSpeak with Mizâdi in southern Imhûlar outside Bârshud's camp of Nisigurûm.\n2\tDefeat Ekhamâti forces on the battlefield (total: 16)\030Place Mizâdi's standard outside the gates of Nisigurûm\030Place Mizâdi's standard in the first encampment of Bârshud's forces\030Place Mizâdi's standard just within the gates of Nisigurûm\tDefeat Ekhamâti and plant Mizâdi's banner in each area.\n3\tRegroup near Mizâdi on the battlefield\tRegroup near Mizâdi on the battlefield.\n4\tSpeak with Mizâdi on the battlefield\tSpeak with Mizâdi on the battlefield.\n",
[11743]="7006EED9\n1\tSearch for Bârshud II near the western tents in Nisigurûm\tSearch for Bârshud II near the red tents to the west in Nisigurûm and challenge him to a duel.\n2\tContinue searching for Bârshud near the eastern tents further in Nisigurûm\tContinue searching for Bârshud II near the eastern tents further in Nisigurûm and challenge him to a duel.\n3\tSearch for Bârshud II near the main tent in Nisigurûm\tSearch for Bârshud II near the main tent in Nisigurûm and challenge him to a duel.\n4\tDefeat Antagâl, Bârshud's Umûni\tDefeat Antagâl, Bârshud's Umûni!\n5\tInterrogate Antagâl about where Bârshud really is\tAntagâl is wounded. He scuttled behind the main tent in Nisigurûm. Interrogate Antagâl about where Bârshud really is.\n6\tFind Mizâdi on the battlefield and give her this grim news\tFind Mizâdi on the battlefield and give her this grim news.\n",
[11744]="70043DF1\n1\tSpeak with Cangoras\030Speak with Edenos\030Speak with Arthon\tGondorian captains can be found in the main strongholds of the Free Peoples. You should speak with the other captains of the Gondorian army.\n",
})
